<file path="docs/design-references/quest-card-ui-1.md">
Create a comprehensive Design System for a gamified self-improvement web application named "Bloom.me". The interface must be minimal, cute, exceptionally user-friendly, clean, and completely in the Thai language. 



Visual & Aesthetic Style:

- 2D Vector style with soft highlights, gradients, and cell-shading to give a pseudo-3D pop-out appearance, heavily inspired by the visual art styles of "Cookie Run Kingdom" and "Angry Birds".

- Color Palette: Eco-friendly and comforting tones. Primary Green (Forest Green, Soft Sage), Clean White, Light Soft Gray background, Charcoal Black for readable typography, and Warm Timber Brown for wooden elements and text contrast.

- Components needed: Neumorphic/Soft-shaded buttons, cute progress bars, rounded card containers with clean drop shadows, and illustrative icon sets for navigation.

- Target Devices: Fully responsive layout adaptive for Mobile, Tablet, and Desktop viewports.

Design a responsive web page layout for "Bloom.me" main dashboard, optimized for both Desktop and Mobile devices. The design is split vertically into scrollable sections using a comforting palette of Green, White, Gray, and Brown. All text labels must be in Thai.



Section 1: Header & Hero Zone (Top of the page)

- Top bar displays "Bloom.me" logo, User Profile with chosen MBTI badge, Tree Level Indicator, and a cute glowing EXP bar showing current progress.

- Right corner features a "ลงชื่อเข้าใช้ / สมัครสมาชิก" button (Sign in/Register) and a "แชร์ต้นไม้" (Share) button.

- Center of the Hero section features a large, beautifully shaded 2D pseudo-3D Tree planted in a customizable pot. 

  * The Tree consists of three distinct growth elements: A robust, thick Trunk (representing Learning/Knowledge), lush green Leaves (representing Physical Health), and blooming colorful Flowers (representing Mental Health).

  * Small pastel-colored "Post-it" memory notes are clipped onto the tree branches.

  * Floating action buttons near the tree: "จัดอันดับ" (Leaderboard) and "เปลี่ยนกระถาง/ตกแต่ง".



Section 2: Quest System & Tasks (Scroll down)

- A beautifully organized tabbed interface splitting tasks into three categories: "ด้านการเรียนรู้" (Knowledge), "ด้านสุขภาพกาย" (Physical Health), and "ด้านสุขภาพจิต" (Mental Health).

- Each tab contains two distinct sub-lists: "เควสประจำวัน" (Daily Quests) and "เควสเสริม" (Side Quests).

- Quest cards feature progress toggles, timer components (for deep focus or fasting), action triggers (like a microphone icon or camera upload shortcut), and clear rewards displaying "Coins" and "EXP".



Section 3: Decoration & Coin Shop (Scroll further down)

- A cute grid-based shop layout using earned Coins to purchase 2D pseudo-3D decorations.

- Categories inside the shop: "รูปปั้นวางบนกระถาง" (Pot Statues), "ของแขวนบนกิ่งไม้" (Branch Hangings), and "ลายโพสอิทสะสม" (Collectible Post-it Designs). Items feature soft shading and shadow depth mimicking the Cookie Run style.



Section 4: About Us (Footer)

- Minimalist footer using clean gray and dark green typography outlining the vision of Bloom.me as a scientific, research-backed habit building platform.

Generate a detailed interactive card UI layout for the Quest Section of the "Bloom.me" web app. Use neat rounded cards with soft borders. All text details must be written in Thai precisely as specified below:



1. ด้านความรู้ (Knowledge) - พัฒนา "ลำต้น" (Trunk Growth):

   - เควสประจำวัน (Daily Quests):

     * "Active Focus (เพ่งสมาธิ)": Card with text input for setting specific learning goals. Backed by Deliberate Practice Theory.

     * "The Deep Root (โหมดจดจ่อ)": Includes a visual 90-minute countdown timer with a 15-20 minute forced rest state selector. Backed by Ultradian Rhythms.

     * "Brain Dump - Voice Edition": Includes a microphone button to record verbal explanations, converting speech-to-text. Backed by The Testing & Production Effect.

     * "Cross-Pollination (ผสมเกสรข้ามศาสตร์)": A scheduling toggle UI to switch study topics every hour. Backed by Interleaved Practice.

     * "Daily Learning Check-in": A locked grayed-out item that unlocks when 1-2 daily tasks are completed. Clicking it opens a "Watering Can" (บัวรดน้ำ) popup.

   - เควสเสริม & ความสำเร็จ (Side Quests & Achievements):

     * "Time Capsule Watering (รดน้ำข้ามเวลา)": Notification bell card for reviewing old topics based on Spacing Effect.

     * "Strategic Delay": Long-term monthly planning calendar view.

     * "Mirror of Truth": Instant feedback action button that unlocks the "กิ่งก้านแห่งปัญญา" item.

     * "The Guardian of Rest": Multi-hour tracking bar. If work exceeds 4-5 hours, it warns the user with a withered tree preview to prevent burnout.

     * "Ten-Year Forest": A continuous login streak calendar tracker.



2. ด้านสุขภาพกาย (Physical Health) - พัฒนา "ใบไม้" (Leaves Growth):

   - เควสประจำวัน (Daily Quests):

     * "Calorie Tracking (นับแคลอรี่)": A split visual gauge bar comparing Calories In (food photo upload/caloric entry) vs Calories Out (Smartwatch integration data tracking steps and distance).

     * "IF System (คุมเวลากิน)": A fasting clock UI showing fasting schedules (e.g., 16:8) synchronized with circadian rhythms.

     * "Sleep Guard (การนอน)": Time picker log for sleep/wake hours. Meeting a 7-8 hour target unlocks a glowing blue shield icon labeled "Cortisol Shield".

     * "Active Recovery & NEAT": A micro-timer that prompts a 5-minute stretching/walking alert automatically after a Deep Focus session ends.

   - Reward Effect: Successful completion rewards a glowing "ละอองแดด (Sunlight Aura)" icon overlay that makes the 2D tree leaves glossily reflective.



3. ด้านสุขภาพจิต (Mental Health) - พัฒนา "ดอกไม้" (Flowers Growth):

   - เควสประจำวัน (Daily Quests):

     * "Daily Mood Check-in": Pop-up window appearing upon entering the game. Includes a text input box for journaling and an AI indicator showing 3 emotion levels: ดี (Good), เฉยๆ (Neutral), ไม่ดี (Bad). Bad emotional patterns trigger a gentle advice overlay. The written text dynamically converts into a Post-it note attached to the center tree.

     * "Adaptive Guidance (ปรับสมดุลใจ)": Contextual activity cards based on mood (e.g., 1-minute deep breathing animation, Sound Therapy audio player, or a Gratitude Journal text field).

   - Reward Effect: Completing the Gratitude Journal triggers an animated "ผีเสื้อแห่งความสงบ (Calm Butterfly)" asset that flies gently around the blooming flowers on the tree.

Design a clean, responsive User Profile and Analytics Dashboard page for "Bloom.me" in Thai language, focusing on clarity, simplicity, and a cute aesthetic.



Component 1: Registration & Initial Setup Form

- Fields for Username, Email, Password, Height (ส่วนสูง ซม.), and Weight (น้ำหนัก กก.).

- An interactive grid for selecting the user's MBTI type (16 personalities), where each selection previews a uniquely styled and colored starting tree variant.



Component 2: Health & Progress Analytics Metrics Area

- Display a card containing the User's Body Mass Index calculated dynamically using standard metric formulas:

- Beside the BMI card, display a dynamic 2D pseudo-3D User Silhouette illustration. The silhouette visually transforms into a fitter, healthier shape depending on the user's logged workout frequency and active step counts.

- Analytics counters with cute custom icons showing: "ชั่วโมงเรียนรู้สะสม" (Accumulated Learning Hours) and "ก้าวเดินสะสม" (Accumulated Steps/Distance synced via Smartwatch).



Component 3: Interactive Progress & Mood Calendar

- A beautiful monthly calendar UI component.

- Each calendar day cell features interactive colored micro-indicators or dots showing how many quests were completed across the 3 categories (Knowledge, Physical, Mental).

- Each day's cell color or emoji icon shifts dynamically to represent the user's logged mood (Good, Neutral, Bad) from their Daily Mood Check-in history. Clicking a day cell expands a modal showing past Post-it text memories and specific quest achievements.

Design a cute, interactive overlay pop-up modal for the "Daily Learning Check-in" feature inside "Bloom.me". The interface language must be in Thai.



Visual Structure:

- The main illustration inside the modal is a beautifully shaded 2D watering can (บัวรดน้ำ).

- Below the illustration, there is a set of 5 sequential slider or star-rating questions:

  1. Goal Clarity: "วันนี้คุณเริ่มต้นการเรียน/ทำงานด้วยเป้าหมายที่ชัดเจนมากแค่ไหน?"

  2. Deep Focus & Flow: "คุณสามารถจดจ่ออยู่กับสิ่งที่ทำโดยไม่ถูกรบกวนได้ดีเพียงใด?"

  3. Active Recall: "วันนี้คุณได้พยายามนึก ทบทวน หรือสรุปสิ่งที่เรียนรู้ด้วยตัวเองมากน้อยแค่ไหน?"

  4. Quality Rest: "คุณได้หยุดพักผ่อนสมองอย่างแท้จริงระหว่างช่วงเรียนหรือทำงานหรือไม่?"

  5. Overall Satisfaction: "โดยรวมแล้ว วันนี้คุณพึงพอใจกับการพัฒนาตัวเองมากแค่ไหน?"

- Optional Bonus Field: "มีอะไรที่อยากปรับปรุงให้ดีขึ้นในวันพรุ่งนี้?" (This specific field content converts into a persistent mini Post-it note on the user interface screen).



Micro-interaction Design:

- As the user slides or gives high star ratings for each question, the water level inside the 2D watering can illustration dynamically fills up with a fluid blue color animation.

- Upon filling out all 5 questions, a primary action button glows. Clicking it plays a visual animation of the watering can tilting and pouring water directly onto the tree's "Trunk" element, accompanied by a glittering light effect (แสงวิบวับ) to signify the tree's expansion and growth.
